#!markdown

# Unknown bits and constraints

`?` represents a bit that may independently be zero or one. Candidate counts
use `BigInteger`; enumeration is always given an explicit upper bound.

#!csharp

#r "nuget: NumeralSystems.Net, 5.1.0"
using NumeralSystems.Net.Type.Incomplete;

var pattern = BitPattern.Parse("1100????");
new {
    Pattern = pattern.ToString(),
    pattern.UnknownBitCount,
    pattern.CandidateCount,
    pattern.MinValue,
    pattern.MaxValue,
    Preview = pattern.EnumerateCandidates(8).ToArray()
}

#!markdown

Solve the constraint `x & 10101010 = 10001000`. The result is another pattern
describing every valid value of `x`.

#!csharp

var solution = BitPattern.SolveAnd(
    BitPattern.Parse("10101010"),
    BitPattern.Parse("10001000"));
solution.ToString()
